ROOT-CAUSE MAP (priority order):
  RC-1 [primary, proven by reproduction A] preflight 'Record runner image' tees into
       ci-logs/ BEFORE any mkdir; the mkdir lives only in the NEXT step, which is skipped
       after the failure. Fix: dedicated bootstrap step immediately after checkout.
  RC-2 [cascade, reproduction B] upload 'ci-logs/**' + if-no-files-found: error then finds
       no files -> second failure. Fix: bootstrap guarantees bootstrap.log; upload the
       directory (not the glob).
  RC-3 [DAG] build-windows/build-linux declare success-only 'needs: preflight' -> both
       SKIPPED when preflight failed (run evidence D). Fix: remove the dependency; keep
       collect-logs as the single aggregator with if: always() && !cancelled().
  RC-4 [gate order] the preflight gates step has a default success condition, so the
       runner-image failure skipped gofmt/tidy/verify. Fix: gates step gets
       if: ${{ !cancelled() }} so independent static gates still run.
  RC-5 [no guaranteed bootstrap evidence in ANY job] build-windows/build-linux/codeql/
       collect-logs create ci-logs only mid-job; an early setup failure would repeat the
       RC-2 cascade there. Fix: bootstrap step in every evidence-producing job.
  RC-6 [artifact identity] per-job artifact names carry no run_attempt; fix names +
       manifest + cleanup matching together.
  RC-7 [collector reporting] deriveFailures can list one job twice (manifest conclusion
       and API conclusion as separate rows) — brief J requires dedup by stable job id with
       both sources shown; the codeql manifest rows must match the API matrix-leg names
       ('analyze (go)'/'analyze (actions)').
  RC-8 [404 classification] the collector must distinguish NEVER_STARTED /
       IN_PROGRESS_AT_SNAPSHOT / API_LOG_UNAVAILABLE / ARTIFACT_MISSING / RECOVERED_FROM_API.
  RC-9 [fallback report] if the collector binary cannot be built, the workflow must still
       write+upload a truthful emergency log.txt (brief 9).
  RC-10 [CodeQL structured records] codeql.yml vet/build steps use raw tee without the
       structured COMMAND record, so a silent successful build has no EXIT_CODE: 0 PASS
       evidence (brief G/47). Fix: run them under scripts/ci/capture.sh.
  RC-11 [GATES NOT REACHED semantics] a failed job that reached no gate must be reported
       as GATES NOT REACHED, not as zero failed gates (brief J/9).
  RC-12 [least privilege] the codeql caller job holds actions: write only because the
       standalone collect job needs it; when called, collect is skipped -> tighten to
       actions: read.
  VERIFIED-ALREADY-GOOD (no change): concurrency cancel-in-progress: false; explicit
  ubuntu-26.04 on every Linux job; $goTags preamble fix in Capture-Step.ps1; CodeQL go
  build-mode manual with traced build AFTER init; distinct SARIF categories; per-job
  always() log uploads; single log.txt artifact design; collector report-before-nonzero-exit.
